Confirmed exact source text; the narrowing failures at lines 436/459 trace to `ConnectorTextBlock.type` being typed as plain `string` (not a literal), so `param.type === 'text'`/`'thinking'` can't structurally exclude it — the only thing that can is the `isConnectorTextBlock` type guard, but it's nested *inside* the unrelated `feature('CONNECTOR_TEXT')` check, so TS can't carry its negation past the `if`. The line-507 error is `AssistantMessage.message.content` being genuinely optional while `hasThinkingContent`'s inline parameter type demands it non-optional.

